 ## Overview
-VoxGRAF is a 3D-aware Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) that replaces the coordinate-based Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) scene representation with a sparse voxel grid generator [S1]. It solves the problem of slow rendering and viewpoint/content entanglement inherent in standard NeRF-like architectures by enabling fast, 3D-consistent image synthesis via a single forward pass [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that rely on neural rendering or reduced sample counts, VoxGRAF leverages sparse voxel grids and trilinear interpolation to maintain high visual fidelity and resolution without sacrificing speed [S1].
+VoxGRAF is a 3D-aware Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) that replaces the coordinate-based Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) scene representation with a sparse voxel grid generator [S1]. It solves the problem of slow rendering and viewpoint/content entanglement inherent in coordinate-based 3D-aware GANs by enabling fast, 3D-consistent image synthesis via a single forward pass [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that rely on neural rendering or reduced sample points, VoxGRAF generates high-resolution geometry directly on a sparse grid, leveraging fast trilinear interpolation to maintain visual fidelity without reducing the number of samples [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-VoxGRAF generates a 3D scene representation conditioned on a latent code and camera pose, then renders it using differentiable volume rendering. The method disentangles the foreground (3D) from the background (2D) to mitigate memory constraints and improve consistency [S1].
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+*   **Inputs:** A latent code $z \in \mathbb{R}^M$ sampled from a standard normal distribution $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$, and a camera pose $\xi$ (extrinsics) and intrinsics $K$ [S1].
+*   **Outputs:** A rendered RGB image $\hat{I}$ and an optional alpha mask $a_r$ [S1].
 
